apers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Differential Geometry\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 22 Oct 2012]\nL9: # Title:N-step energy of maps and fixed-point property of random groups\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite5†Hiroyasu Izeki , cite6†Takefumi Kondo , cite7†Shin Nayatani L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled N-step energy of maps and fixed-point property of random groups, by Hiroyasu Izeki and 1 other authors\nL14: \nL15: cite8†View PDF cite9†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We prove that a random group of the graph model associated with a sequence of expanders has fixed-point property for a certain class of CAT(0) spaces. We use Gromov's criterion for fixed-point property in terms of the growth of n-step energy of equivariant maps from a finitely generated group into a CAT(0) space, to which we give a detailed proof.\nL17: We estimate a relevant geometric invariant of the tangent cones of the Euclidean buildings associated with the groups PGL(m,Q_r), and deduce from the general result above that the same random group has fixed-point property for all of these Euclidean buildings with m bounded from above.\nL18: Subjects:  | Differential Geometry (math.DG); Group Theory (math.GR)\nL19: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 20F65 (Primary) 58E20, 20P05 (Secondary)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite10†arXiv:1210.5829 [math.DG]\nL21:    | (or cite11†arXiv:1210.5829v1 [math.DG] for this version)\nL22:    | cite12†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1210.5829†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Hiroyasu Izeki [cite13†view email ]\nL26: [v1] Mon, 22 Oct 2012 08:18:23 UTC (31 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled N-step energy of maps and fixed-point property of random groups, by Hiroyasu Izeki and 1 other authors\nL33: \nL34: 